#!/usr/bin/env python3
# wiki-extension: Say what failed in GitLab CI and why, and note in the wiki when it is fixed.
# wiki-events: tick
# wiki-setup: yes
# wiki-settings: yes
# wiki-detect: .gitlab-ci.yml remote:gitlab
"""wiki gitlab: an llm-wiki extension. Standard library only.

For agents that have no CI watching of their own. It asks GitLab, through the glab program, which
pipelines are failing in a clone's project, and why: the failing job, the first line that looks
like the error, and a short excerpt of that job's log, kept on this machine. With a folder watched,
the tick event leaves a line for the next session on that branch when a pipeline starts failing,
and can save a note in the wiki when the failure is fixed.

It only READS GitLab, and it writes nothing anywhere: every call is `glab api` with the method GET,
plus `glab auth status`. It never starts, retries or cancels a pipeline, never pushes, and starts no
agent to fix anything. It never reads, asks for, prints or stores a token: glab holds the sign-in.
"""
